window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b371-5e780dc573d4ef04.json"]={sha256:"5e780dc573d4ef04a1bacb47d65cb059cee80fbd9f199abb5cf9eb0f082e9ca0",value:{"id":"b371","title":"歐洲列車控制系統整合","titleEn":"European Train Control System integration","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課聚焦歐洲列控版本介面與車地相容驗證。從列控制動模型輸入建立物理或資訊邊界，接著把車地資料交接與介面失配頂事件連成可驗證的介面，最後以互通試驗推論範圍整理證據。學徒逐一完成機制推導、數值算例、失效辨識及參數實驗，所有練習限定在離線模型或隔離教具，保留假設與量測的不確定度。","summaryEn":"This course studies european train-control version interfaces and train–track compatibility. Start with train-control braking-model inputs to define physical or information boundaries, connect train–track data handoff with top event for interface mismatch as verifiable interfaces, and organize evidence through scope of interoperability inference. Each unit develops a mechanism, numerical example, failure diagnosis and parameter experiment in an offline model or isolated teaching rig, retaining assumptions and measurement uncertainty.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-control","subcategoryTitle":"號誌與營運控制","subcategoryTitleEn":"Signalling and operational control","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-control","learningTags":["rail","rail-control","control"],"architectureFamily":"rail-control","architectureNodes":[["地標參考","Balise reference"],["車載版本","Onboard version"],["地面版本","Trackside version"],["模式機器","Mode machine"],["相容證據","Compatibility evidence"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-control","labels":["地標參考","車載版本","地面版本","模式機器","相容證據"],"labelsEn":["Balise reference","Onboard version","Trackside version","Mode machine","Compatibility evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創整合工作單，所有輸入均為教學假設而非代表工程實測：先研究列控制動模型輸入。原創假想教學輸入：初速 v=20 m/s；定減速度大小 a=0.8 m/s2；反應時間 tau=1.5 s。公式 y=v*tau+v*v/(2*a)，代入得 y=280 m。邊界：平直路線、定減速度、無輪滑；未含坡度、黏著變動或制動建立曲線。敏感度只改 v=20 至 22 m/s，輸出變為 335.5 m；離散計數採整數變化。再獨立研究應答器位置與時效：原創假想教學輸入：列車速度 v=18 m/s；資料年齡 t=0.25 s；定位誤差界 e=0.6 m。公式 y=v*t+e，代入得 y=5.1 m。邊界：定速與有界誤差的保守加總，非隨機誤差的均方根合成。兩個結果不能因同一課程就任意相加，必須先確認單位、因果順序及共同邊界。本單元以簡化制動距離理解速度、反應時間與減速度的角色，避免將教材算例當成列控制動曲線。最後提出一項量測能區分模型假設失效與儀器偏差，將輸入表、重算結果和適用限制一併交付。","textEn":"Original integrated worksheet; every input is a teaching assumption rather than a measurement from a reference project. First investigate train-control braking-model inputs. Original hypothetical teaching inputs: initial speed v=20 m/s; constant deceleration magnitude a=0.8 m/s2; response time tau=1.5 s. Formula y=v*tau+v*v/(2*a) gives y=280 m. Boundary: Level track, constant deceleration and no slip; gradients, adhesion variation and brake build-up curves are excluded. For sensitivity, change only v=20 to 22 m/s; the output becomes 335.5 m. Discrete counts use whole-number steps. Independently investigate balise position and data freshness: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: train speed v=18 m/s; data age t=0.25 s; position error bound e=0.6 m. Formula y=v*t+e gives y=5.1 m. Boundary: Constant speed and a conservative sum of bounded errors, not root-sum-square combination of random errors. Results cannot be added merely because they belong to the same course: check units, causal sequence and shared boundaries first. Use simplified stopping distance to understand speed, response and deceleration, without treating a teaching calculation as an operational ETCS braking curve. Propose one measurement distinguishing a failed model assumption from instrument bias, and deliver the input table, recomputed results and applicability limits together.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b371-v16-s1","title":"列控制動模型輸入與應答器位置與時效","titleEn":"Train-control braking-model inputs & Balise position and data freshness","description":"本階段聚焦「列控制動模型輸入」與「應答器位置與時效」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Train-control braking-model inputs\" and \"Balise position and data freshness\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b371-v16-01","title":"列控制動模型輸入：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Train-control braking-model inputs: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「列控制動模型輸入」如何影響歐洲列車控制系統整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Train-control braking-model inputs” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “European Train Control System integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元以簡化制動距離理解速度、反應時間與減速度的角色，避免將教材算例當成列控制動曲線。停止距離由反應期間的等速前進與制動期間的動能消散相加。速度增加會同時增加兩項，而減速度只影響第二項；把控制命令發出時間當成制動力建立時間會漏掉一段距離。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：平直路線、定減速度、無輪滑；未含坡度、黏著變動或制動建立曲線。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「列控制動模型輸入」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use simplified stopping distance to understand speed, response and deceleration, without treating a teaching calculation as an operational ETCS braking curve. Stopping distance combines constant-speed travel during response with kinetic-energy removal during braking. Speed changes both contributions, whereas deceleration changes only the second. A command timestamp is not the instant at which the full braking force becomes available. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Level track, constant deceleration and no slip; gradients, adhesion variation and brake build-up curves are excluded. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Train-control braking-model inputs” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：初速 v=20 m/s；定減速度大小 a=0.8 m/s2；反應時間 tau=1.5 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: initial speed v=20 m/s; constant deceleration magnitude a=0.8 m/s2; response time tau=1.5 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「速度提高一成時停止距離也必定只增加一成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Increasing speed by ten percent always increases stopping distance by exactly ten percent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「列控制動模型輸入」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Train-control braking-model inputs”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-01-k1","title":"列控制動模型輸入","titleEn":"Train-control braking-model inputs","text":"本單元以簡化制動距離理解速度、反應時間與減速度的角色，避免將教材算例當成列控制動曲線。停止距離由反應期間的等速前進與制動期間的動能消散相加。","textEn":"Use simplified stopping distance to understand speed, response and deceleration, without treating a teaching calculation as an operational ETCS braking curve. Stopping distance combines constant-speed travel during response with kinetic-energy removal during braking.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：速度提高一成時停止距離也必定只增加一成 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Increasing speed by ten percent always increases stopping distance by exactly ten percent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「列控制動模型輸入」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Train-control braking-model inputs\" is correct?","options":["速度提高一成時停止距離也必定只增加一成","本單元以簡化制動距離理解速度、反應時間與減速度的角色，避免將教材算例當成列控制動曲線。","封包剛收到就代表其中位置一定是現在的位置"],"optionsEn":["Increasing speed by ten percent always increases stopping distance by exactly ten percent.","Use simplified stopping distance to understand speed, response and deceleration, without treating a teaching calculation as an operational ETCS braking curve.","A newly received packet always contains the present position."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以簡化制動距離理解速度、反應時間與減速度的角色，避免將教材算例當成列控制動曲線。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use simplified stopping distance to understand speed, response and deceleration, without treating a teaching calculation as an operational ETCS braking curve. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b371-v16-02","title":"列控制動模型輸入：定量估算","titleEn":"Train-control braking-model inputs: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「列控制動模型輸入」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Train-control braking-model inputs” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：初速 v=20 m/s；定減速度大小 a=0.8 m/s2；反應時間 tau=1.5 s。公式 y=v*tau+v*v/(2*a)，代入得 y=280 m。邊界：平直路線、定減速度、無輪滑；未含坡度、黏著變動或制動建立曲線。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: initial speed v=20 m/s; constant deceleration magnitude a=0.8 m/s2; response time tau=1.5 s. Formula y=v*tau+v*v/(2*a) gives y=280 m. Boundary: Level track, constant deceleration and no slip; gradients, adhesion variation and brake build-up curves are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同一時基記錄速度、制動命令與加速度，分別積分反應段及減速段，再與實際位移比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record speed, brake command and acceleration on one clock, integrate response and deceleration separately, and compare their sum with measured displacement.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：初速 v=20 m/s；定減速度大小 a=0.8 m/s2；反應時間 tau=1.5 s。公式 y=v*tau+v*v/(2*a)，代入得 y=280 m。邊界：平直路線、定減速度、無輪滑；未含坡度、黏著變動或制動建立曲線。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: initial speed v=20 m/s; constant deceleration magnitude a=0.8 m/s2; response time tau=1.5 s. Formula y=v*tau+v*v/(2*a) gives y=280 m. Boundary: Level track, constant deceleration and no slip; gradients, adhesion variation and brake build-up curves are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「列控制動模型輸入」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Train-control braking-model inputs\", which statement holds?","options":["每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","原創假想教學輸入：初速 v=20 m/s；定減速度大小 a=0.8 m/s2；反應時間 tau=1.5 s。"],"optionsEn":["Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: initial speed v=20 m/s; constant deceleration magnitude a=0.8 m/s2; response time tau=1.5 s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：初速 v=20 m/s；定減速度大小 a=0.8 m/s2；反應時間 tau=1.5 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: initial speed v=20 m/s; constant deceleration magnitude a=0.8 m/s2; response time tau=1.5 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b371-v16-03","title":"列控制動模型輸入：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Train-control braking-model inputs: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「列控制動模型輸入」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Train-control braking-model inputs” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同一時基記錄速度、制動命令與加速度，分別積分反應段及減速段，再與實際位移比較。以「列控制動模型輸入」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record speed, brake command and acceleration on one clock, integrate response and deceleration separately, and compare their sum with measured displacement. For train-control braking-model inputs, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把初速 v 從 20 改成 22 m/s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 280 變為 335.5 m。先說明「列控制動模型輸入」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only initial speed v from 20 to 22 m/s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 280 to 335.5 m. Explain the causal direction for train-control braking-model inputs, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：減速度偏低與反應延遲都會使停車超出目標，但速度曲線的起始轉折可以區分兩種原因。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Weak deceleration and delayed response both cause an overrun, but the onset of the speed-curve change distinguishes these causes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同一時基記錄速度、制動命令與加速度，分別積分反應段及減速段，再與實際位移比較。以「列控制動模型輸入」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Record speed, brake command and acceleration on one clock, integrate response and deceleration separately, and compare their sum with measured displacement. For train-control braking-model inputs, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把初速 v 從 20 改成 22 m/s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 280 變為 335.5 m。先說明「列控制動模型輸入」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only initial speed v from 20 to 22 m/s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 280 to 335.5 m. Explain the causal direction for train-control braking-model inputs, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「列控制動模型輸入」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Train-control braking-model inputs\"?","options":["以同一時基記錄速度、制動命令與加速度，分別積分反應段及減速段，再與實際位移比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致"],"optionsEn":["Record speed, brake command and acceleration on one clock, integrate response and deceleration separately, and compare their sum with measured displacement.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以同一時基記錄速度、制動命令與加速度，分別積分反應段及減速段，再與實際位移比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record speed, brake command and acceleration on one clock, integrate response and deceleration separately, and compare their sum with measured displacement. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b371-v16-04","title":"列控制動模型輸入：失效診斷","titleEn":"Train-control braking-model inputs: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「列控制動模型輸入」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Train-control braking-model inputs” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"減速度偏低與反應延遲都會使停車超出目標，但速度曲線的起始轉折可以區分兩種原因。回到「列控制動模型輸入」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Weak deceleration and delayed response both cause an overrun, but the onset of the speed-curve change distinguishes these causes. Trace the input chain for train-control braking-model inputs. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：平直路線、定減速度、無輪滑；未含坡度、黏著變動或制動建立曲線。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Level track, constant deceleration and no slip; gradients, adhesion variation and brake build-up curves are excluded.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「速度提高一成時停止距離也必定只增加一成」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Increasing speed by ten percent always increases stopping distance by exactly ten percent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"減速度偏低與反應延遲都會使停車超出目標，但速度曲線的起始轉折可以區分兩種原因。回到「列控制動模型輸入」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Weak deceleration and delayed response both cause an overrun, but the onset of the speed-curve change distinguishes these causes. Trace the input chain for train-control braking-model inputs. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「列控制動模型輸入」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Train-control braking-model inputs\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","減速度偏低與反應延遲都會使停車超出目標，但速度曲線的起始轉折可以區分兩種原因。","封包剛收到就代表其中位置一定是現在的位置"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Weak deceleration and delayed response both cause an overrun, but the onset of the speed-curve change distinguishes these causes.","A newly received packet always contains the present position."],"answer":1,"explanation":"減速度偏低與反應延遲都會使停車超出目標，但速度曲線的起始轉折可以區分兩種原因。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Weak deceleration and delayed response both cause an overrun, but the onset of the speed-curve change distinguishes these causes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b371-v16-05","title":"應答器位置與時效：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Balise position and data freshness: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「應答器位置與時效」如何影響歐洲列車控制系統整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Balise position and data freshness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “European Train Control System integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元區分地標參考點的定位誤差與車載處理時間，追蹤資料從讀取到採用的整個路徑。位置資料的數值誤差與資料變舊造成的位移應分開處理。即使感測器本身準確，封包等待與處理延遲仍會擴大當前位置的不確定範圍；接收時間不能取代量測時間，否則不同子系統可能各自認為資料是新的。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：定速與有界誤差的保守加總，非隨機誤差的均方根合成。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「應答器位置與時效」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate reference-point uncertainty from onboard processing time, tracing the complete path from landmark reading to use in the train-control calculation. Position measurement error and displacement accumulated while data ages are separate contributions. Even an accurate sensor can yield an uncertain current location after queuing and processing delays. Reception time cannot substitute for measurement time because subsystems could then each mistakenly regard stale information as new. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Constant speed and a conservative sum of bounded errors, not root-sum-square combination of random errors. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Balise position and data freshness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：列車速度 v=18 m/s；資料年齡 t=0.25 s；定位誤差界 e=0.6 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: train speed v=18 m/s; data age t=0.25 s; position error bound e=0.6 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「封包剛收到就代表其中位置一定是現在的位置」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A newly received packet always contains the present position.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「應答器位置與時效」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Balise position and data freshness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-05-k1","title":"應答器位置與時效","titleEn":"Balise position and data freshness","text":"本單元區分地標參考點的定位誤差與車載處理時間，追蹤資料從讀取到採用的整個路徑。位置資料的數值誤差與資料變舊造成的位移應分開處理。","textEn":"Separate reference-point uncertainty from onboard processing time, tracing the complete path from landmark reading to use in the train-control calculation. Position measurement error and displacement accumulated while data ages are separate contributions.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：封包剛收到就代表其中位置一定是現在的位置 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A newly received packet always contains the present position. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「應答器位置與時效」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Balise position and data freshness\" is correct?","options":["封包剛收到就代表其中位置一定是現在的位置","短距離校正準確就能保證長距離里程也完全準確","本單元區分地標參考點的定位誤差與車載處理時間，追蹤資料從讀取到採用的整個路徑。"],"optionsEn":["A newly received packet always contains the present position.","Accurate short-distance calibration guarantees perfectly accurate long-distance odometry.","Separate reference-point uncertainty from onboard processing time, tracing the complete path from landmark reading to use in the train-control calculation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元區分地標參考點的定位誤差與車載處理時間，追蹤資料從讀取到採用的整個路徑。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate reference-point uncertainty from onboard processing time, tracing the complete path from landmark reading to use in the train-control calculation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b371-v16-06","title":"應答器位置與時效：定量估算","titleEn":"Balise position and data freshness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「應答器位置與時效」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Balise position and data freshness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：列車速度 v=18 m/s；資料年齡 t=0.25 s；定位誤差界 e=0.6 m。公式 y=v*t+e，代入得 y=5.1 m。邊界：定速與有界誤差的保守加總，非隨機誤差的均方根合成。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: train speed v=18 m/s; data age t=0.25 s; position error bound e=0.6 m. Formula y=v*t+e gives y=5.1 m. Boundary: Constant speed and a conservative sum of bounded errors, not root-sum-square combination of random errors. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保留量測、傳送及接收三個時間戳，以延遲注入重播檢查界限是否包住真值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Preserve measurement, transmit and receive timestamps; replay injected delays and verify that the resulting bound encloses the reference position.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：列車速度 v=18 m/s；資料年齡 t=0.25 s；定位誤差界 e=0.6 m。公式 y=v*t+e，代入得 y=5.1 m。邊界：定速與有界誤差的保守加總，非隨機誤差的均方根合成。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: train speed v=18 m/s; data age t=0.25 s; position error bound e=0.6 m. Formula y=v*t+e gives y=5.1 m. Boundary: Constant speed and a conservative sum of bounded errors, not root-sum-square combination of random errors.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「應答器位置與時效」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Balise position and data freshness\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：列車速度 v=18 m/s；資料年齡 t=0.25 s；定位誤差界 e=0.6 m。","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合","任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: train speed v=18 m/s; data age t=0.25 s; position error bound e=0.6 m.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.","If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：列車速度 v=18 m/s；資料年齡 t=0.25 s；定位誤差界 e=0.6 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: train speed v=18 m/s; data age t=0.25 s; position error bound e=0.6 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b371-v16-07","title":"應答器位置與時效：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Balise position and data freshness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「應答器位置與時效」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Balise position and data freshness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保留量測、傳送及接收三個時間戳，以延遲注入重播檢查界限是否包住真值。以「應答器位置與時效」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Preserve measurement, transmit and receive timestamps; replay injected delays and verify that the resulting bound encloses the reference position. For balise position and data freshness, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把資料年齡 t 從 0.25 改成 0.275 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 5.1 變為 5.55 m。先說明「應答器位置與時效」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only data age t from 0.25 to 0.275 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 5.1 to 5.55 m. Explain the causal direction for balise position and data freshness, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：時鐘偏移會偽裝成網路延遲，重設時間戳又可能隱藏陳舊資料，需用獨立時間基準辨認。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Clock offset can imitate network delay, while timestamp replacement can conceal stale data; an independent time reference distinguishes them. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保留量測、傳送及接收三個時間戳，以延遲注入重播檢查界限是否包住真值。以「應答器位置與時效」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Preserve measurement, transmit and receive timestamps; replay injected delays and verify that the resulting bound encloses the reference position. For balise position and data freshness, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把資料年齡 t 從 0.25 改成 0.275 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 5.1 變為 5.55 m。先說明「應答器位置與時效」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only data age t from 0.25 to 0.275 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 5.1 to 5.55 m. Explain the causal direction for balise position and data freshness, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「應答器位置與時效」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Balise position and data freshness\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","保留量測、傳送及接收三個時間戳，以延遲注入重播檢查界限是否包住真值。","所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Preserve measurement, transmit and receive timestamps; replay injected delays and verify that the resulting bound encloses the reference position.","All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results."],"answer":1,"explanation":"保留量測、傳送及接收三個時間戳，以延遲注入重播檢查界限是否包住真值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Preserve measurement, transmit and receive timestamps; replay injected delays and verify that the resulting bound encloses the reference position. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b371-v16-08","title":"應答器位置與時效：失效診斷","titleEn":"Balise position and data freshness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「應答器位置與時效」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Balise position and data freshness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"時鐘偏移會偽裝成網路延遲，重設時間戳又可能隱藏陳舊資料，需用獨立時間基準辨認。回到「應答器位置與時效」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Clock offset can imitate network delay, while timestamp replacement can conceal stale data; an independent time reference distinguishes them. Trace the input chain for balise position and data freshness. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：定速與有界誤差的保守加總，非隨機誤差的均方根合成。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Constant speed and a conservative sum of bounded errors, not root-sum-square combination of random errors.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「封包剛收到就代表其中位置一定是現在的位置」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A newly received packet always contains the present position.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"時鐘偏移會偽裝成網路延遲，重設時間戳又可能隱藏陳舊資料，需用獨立時間基準辨認。回到「應答器位置與時效」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Clock offset can imitate network delay, while timestamp replacement can conceal stale data; an independent time reference distinguishes them. Trace the input chain for balise position and data freshness. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「應答器位置與時效」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Balise position and data freshness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","短距離校正準確就能保證長距離里程也完全準確","時鐘偏移會偽裝成網路延遲，重設時間戳又可能隱藏陳舊資料，需用獨立時間基準辨認。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Accurate short-distance calibration guarantees perfectly accurate long-distance odometry.","Clock offset can imitate network delay, while timestamp replacement can conceal stale data; an independent time reference distinguishes them."],"answer":2,"explanation":"時鐘偏移會偽裝成網路延遲，重設時間戳又可能隱藏陳舊資料，需用獨立時間基準辨認。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Clock offset can imitate network delay, while timestamp replacement can conceal stale data; an independent time reference distinguishes them. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b371-v16-s2","title":"應答器間里程漂移與車地資料交接","titleEn":"Odometry drift between balises & Train–track data handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「應答器間里程漂移」與「車地資料交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Odometry drift between balises\" and \"Train–track data handoff\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b371-v16-09","title":"應答器間里程漂移：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Odometry drift between balises: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「應答器間里程漂移」如何影響歐洲列車控制系統整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Odometry drift between balises” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “European Train Control System integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元比較兩個地標之間的距離累積誤差，將輪徑比例偏差與單次地標校正偏移分開。輪徑與脈衝換算比例的誤差會隨行走距離累積，固定零點偏差則不隨距離放大。輪滑與空轉使輪周距離不等於地面位移；定期地標校正能約束累積誤差，但地標本身的位置與辨識可信度仍須驗證。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：固定比例誤差與固定偏移，未包含時變輪滑或輪徑磨耗歷程。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「應答器間里程漂移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compare distance accumulation between landmarks, separating wheel-scale bias from the one-time offset introduced by a landmark correction. Wheel diameter and pulse-scale error accumulate with distance, whereas a fixed zero offset does not grow. Slip makes wheel travel differ from ground displacement. Landmark updates can constrain drift, but the landmark position and identification credibility still require verification. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Constant scale error plus fixed offset; variable slip and wheel-wear history are not modelled. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Odometry drift between balises” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：行走距離 distance=1500 m；比例誤差 scale=0.004 1；固定偏差 bias=0.2 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: travelled distance distance=1500 m; scale error scale=0.004 1; fixed offset bias=0.2 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「短距離校正準確就能保證長距離里程也完全準確」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Accurate short-distance calibration guarantees perfectly accurate long-distance odometry.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「應答器間里程漂移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Odometry drift between balises”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-09-k1","title":"應答器間里程漂移","titleEn":"Odometry drift between balises","text":"本單元比較兩個地標之間的距離累積誤差，將輪徑比例偏差與單次地標校正偏移分開。輪徑與脈衝換算比例的誤差會隨行走距離累積，固定零點偏差則不隨距離放大。","textEn":"Compare distance accumulation between landmarks, separating wheel-scale bias from the one-time offset introduced by a landmark correction. Wheel diameter and pulse-scale error accumulate with distance, whereas a fixed zero offset does not grow.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：短距離校正準確就能保證長距離里程也完全準確 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Accurate short-distance calibration guarantees perfectly accurate long-distance odometry. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「應答器間里程漂移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Odometry drift between balises\" is correct?","options":["本單元比較兩個地標之間的距離累積誤差，將輪徑比例偏差與單次地標校正偏移分開。","短距離校正準確就能保證長距離里程也完全準確","每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短"],"optionsEn":["Compare distance accumulation between landmarks, separating wheel-scale bias from the one-time offset introduced by a landmark correction.","Accurate short-distance calibration guarantees perfectly accurate long-distance odometry.","Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元比較兩個地標之間的距離累積誤差，將輪徑比例偏差與單次地標校正偏移分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compare distance accumulation between landmarks, separating wheel-scale bias from the one-time offset introduced by a landmark correction. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b371-v16-10","title":"應答器間里程漂移：定量估算","titleEn":"Odometry drift between balises: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「應答器間里程漂移」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Odometry drift between balises” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：行走距離 distance=1500 m；比例誤差 scale=0.004 1；固定偏差 bias=0.2 m。公式 y=distance*scale+bias，代入得 y=6.2 m。邊界：固定比例誤差與固定偏移，未包含時變輪滑或輪徑磨耗歷程。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: travelled distance distance=1500 m; scale error scale=0.004 1; fixed offset bias=0.2 m. Formula y=distance*scale+bias gives y=6.2 m. Boundary: Constant scale error plus fixed offset; variable slip and wheel-wear history are not modelled. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在多個已知距離區段繪製殘差對距離，利用斜率與截距分別估計比例及零點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot residual against several known travel distances and use slope and intercept to separate scale and zero-offset effects.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：行走距離 distance=1500 m；比例誤差 scale=0.004 1；固定偏差 bias=0.2 m。公式 y=distance*scale+bias，代入得 y=6.2 m。邊界：固定比例誤差與固定偏移，未包含時變輪滑或輪徑磨耗歷程。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: travelled distance distance=1500 m; scale error scale=0.004 1; fixed offset bias=0.2 m. Formula y=distance*scale+bias gives y=6.2 m. Boundary: Constant scale error plus fixed offset; variable slip and wheel-wear history are not modelled.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「應答器間里程漂移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Odometry drift between balises\", which statement holds?","options":["測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","原創假想教學輸入：行走距離 distance=1500 m；比例誤差 scale=0.004 1；固定偏差 bias=0.2 m。","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致"],"optionsEn":["One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: travelled distance distance=1500 m; scale error scale=0.004 1; fixed offset bias=0.2 m.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：行走距離 distance=1500 m；比例誤差 scale=0.004 1；固定偏差 bias=0.2 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: travelled distance distance=1500 m; scale error scale=0.004 1; fixed offset bias=0.2 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b371-v16-11","title":"應答器間里程漂移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Odometry drift between balises: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「應答器間里程漂移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Odometry drift between balises” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在多個已知距離區段繪製殘差對距離，利用斜率與截距分別估計比例及零點。以「應答器間里程漂移」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot residual against several known travel distances and use slope and intercept to separate scale and zero-offset effects. For odometry drift between balises, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把行走距離 distance 從 1500 改成 1650 m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 6.2 變為 6.8 m。先說明「應答器間里程漂移」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only travelled distance distance from 1500 to 1650 m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 6.2 to 6.8 m. Explain the causal direction for odometry drift between balises, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：一次短距離校正可能掩蓋比例誤差，輪滑事件則在殘差曲線留下突跳而非固定斜率。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A short calibration run can hide scale error; slip events cause residual jumps rather than a constant slope. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在多個已知距離區段繪製殘差對距離，利用斜率與截距分別估計比例及零點。以「應答器間里程漂移」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Plot residual against several known travel distances and use slope and intercept to separate scale and zero-offset effects. For odometry drift between balises, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把行走距離 distance 從 1500 改成 1650 m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 6.2 變為 6.8 m。先說明「應答器間里程漂移」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only travelled distance distance from 1500 to 1650 m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 6.2 to 6.8 m. Explain the causal direction for odometry drift between balises, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「應答器間里程漂移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Odometry drift between balises\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零","在多個已知距離區段繪製殘差對距離，利用斜率與截距分別估計比例及零點。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero.","Plot residual against several known travel distances and use slope and intercept to separate scale and zero-offset effects."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在多個已知距離區段繪製殘差對距離，利用斜率與截距分別估計比例及零點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot residual against several known travel distances and use slope and intercept to separate scale and zero-offset effects. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b371-v16-12","title":"應答器間里程漂移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Odometry drift between balises: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「應答器間里程漂移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Odometry drift between balises” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"一次短距離校正可能掩蓋比例誤差，輪滑事件則在殘差曲線留下突跳而非固定斜率。回到「應答器間里程漂移」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A short calibration run can hide scale error; slip events cause residual jumps rather than a constant slope. Trace the input chain for odometry drift between balises. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：固定比例誤差與固定偏移，未包含時變輪滑或輪徑磨耗歷程。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Constant scale error plus fixed offset; variable slip and wheel-wear history are not modelled.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「短距離校正準確就能保證長距離里程也完全準確」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Accurate short-distance calibration guarantees perfectly accurate long-distance odometry.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"一次短距離校正可能掩蓋比例誤差，輪滑事件則在殘差曲線留下突跳而非固定斜率。回到「應答器間里程漂移」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"A short calibration run can hide scale error; slip events cause residual jumps rather than a constant slope. Trace the input chain for odometry drift between balises. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「應答器間里程漂移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Odometry drift between balises\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["一次短距離校正可能掩蓋比例誤差，輪滑事件則在殘差曲線留下突跳而非固定斜率。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短"],"optionsEn":["A short calibration run can hide scale error; slip events cause residual jumps rather than a constant slope.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay."],"answer":0,"explanation":"一次短距離校正可能掩蓋比例誤差，輪滑事件則在殘差曲線留下突跳而非固定斜率。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A short calibration run can hide scale error; slip events cause residual jumps rather than a constant slope. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b371-v16-13","title":"車地資料交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Train–track data handoff: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「車地資料交接」如何影響歐洲列車控制系統整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Train–track data handoff” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “European Train Control System integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元為讀取、驗證、轉換與採用定義一致起訖，確保各供應商的介面延遲不會漏算。端到端延遲由量測、通訊、運算與致動串接而成。改善最快的一段通常影響有限，且平均延遲不能代表最壞尾端；定義一致的起訖事件，才能避免子系統都量到好看的數值卻漏掉交接等待。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：各階段串行且時間確定，沒有平行重疊或隨機尾端。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「車地資料交接」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Define consistent start and finish events for reading, validation, conversion and use so interface latency between suppliers is not omitted. End-to-end delay spans sensing, communication, computation and actuation. Improving the fastest stage often yields little benefit, and mean latency does not represent its worst tail. Consistent start and end events prevent subsystems from reporting attractive numbers while overlooking handoff queues. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Deterministic serial stages without overlap or random latency tails. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Train–track data handoff” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：量測時間 sense=0.03 s；網路時間 network=0.08 s；運算時間 compute=0.02 s；致動時間 actuate=0.12 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensing time sense=0.03 s; network time network=0.08 s; computation time compute=0.02 s; actuation time actuate=0.12 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「車地資料交接」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Train–track data handoff”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-13-k1","title":"車地資料交接","titleEn":"Train–track data handoff","text":"本單元為讀取、驗證、轉換與採用定義一致起訖，確保各供應商的介面延遲不會漏算。端到端延遲由量測、通訊、運算與致動串接而成。","textEn":"Define consistent start and finish events for reading, validation, conversion and use so interface latency between suppliers is not omitted. End-to-end delay spans sensing, communication, computation and actuation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「車地資料交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Train–track data handoff\" is correct?","options":["每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短","本單元為讀取、驗證、轉換與採用定義一致起訖，確保各供應商的介面延遲不會漏算。","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合"],"optionsEn":["Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay.","Define consistent start and finish events for reading, validation, conversion and use so interface latency between suppliers is not omitted.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元為讀取、驗證、轉換與採用定義一致起訖，確保各供應商的介面延遲不會漏算。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Define consistent start and finish events for reading, validation, conversion and use so interface latency between suppliers is not omitted. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b371-v16-14","title":"車地資料交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Train–track data handoff: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「車地資料交接」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Train–track data handoff” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：量測時間 sense=0.03 s；網路時間 network=0.08 s；運算時間 compute=0.02 s；致動時間 actuate=0.12 s。公式 y=sense+network+compute+actuate，代入得 y=0.25 s。邊界：各階段串行且時間確定，沒有平行重疊或隨機尾端。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensing time sense=0.03 s; network time network=0.08 s; computation time compute=0.02 s; actuation time actuate=0.12 s. Formula y=sense+network+compute+actuate gives y=0.25 s. Boundary: Deterministic serial stages without overlap or random latency tails. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿同一事件編號串接時間戳，檢查每一段邊界是否重疊或漏算，並注入負載重測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Follow one event identifier through timestamps, check stage boundaries for overlap or gaps, and repeat under injected load.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：量測時間 sense=0.03 s；網路時間 network=0.08 s；運算時間 compute=0.02 s；致動時間 actuate=0.12 s。公式 y=sense+network+compute+actuate，代入得 y=0.25 s。邊界：各階段串行且時間確定，沒有平行重疊或隨機尾端。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensing time sense=0.03 s; network time network=0.08 s; computation time compute=0.02 s; actuation time actuate=0.12 s. Formula y=sense+network+compute+actuate gives y=0.25 s. Boundary: Deterministic serial stages without overlap or random latency tails.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「車地資料交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Train–track data handoff\", which statement holds?","options":["任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘","所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果","原創假想教學輸入：量測時間 sense=0.03 s。"],"optionsEn":["If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product.","All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensing time sense=0.03 s; network time network=0.08 s; computation time compute=0.02 s; actuation time actuate=0.12 s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：量測時間 sense=0.03 s；網路時間 network=0.08 s；運算時間 compute=0.02 s；致動時間 actuate=0.12 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensing time sense=0.03 s; network time network=0.08 s; computation time compute=0.02 s; actuation time actuate=0.12 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b371-v16-15","title":"車地資料交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Train–track data handoff: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「車地資料交接」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Train–track data handoff” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿同一事件編號串接時間戳，檢查每一段邊界是否重疊或漏算，並注入負載重測。以「車地資料交接」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Follow one event identifier through timestamps, check stage boundaries for overlap or gaps, and repeat under injected load. For train–track data handoff, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把網路時間 network 從 0.08 改成 0.088 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.25 變為 0.258 s。先說明「車地資料交接」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only network time network from 0.08 to 0.088 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.25 to 0.258 s. Explain the causal direction for train–track data handoff, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：時間基準不同可造成負延遲假象；漏記排隊會使快速單元測試無法預測整合表現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Different clock references can create apparently negative delays; omitted queues prevent fast unit tests from predicting integrated performance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿同一事件編號串接時間戳，檢查每一段邊界是否重疊或漏算，並注入負載重測。以「車地資料交接」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Follow one event identifier through timestamps, check stage boundaries for overlap or gaps, and repeat under injected load. For train–track data handoff, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把網路時間 network 從 0.08 改成 0.088 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.25 變為 0.258 s。先說明「車地資料交接」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only network time network from 0.08 to 0.088 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.25 to 0.258 s. Explain the causal direction for train–track data handoff, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「車地資料交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Train–track data handoff\"?","options":["沿同一事件編號串接時間戳，檢查每一段邊界是否重疊或漏算，並注入負載重測。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","速度提高一成時停止距離也必定只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["Follow one event identifier through timestamps, check stage boundaries for overlap or gaps, and repeat under injected load.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Increasing speed by ten percent always increases stopping distance by exactly ten percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沿同一事件編號串接時間戳，檢查每一段邊界是否重疊或漏算，並注入負載重測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Follow one event identifier through timestamps, check stage boundaries for overlap or gaps, and repeat under injected load. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b371-v16-16","title":"車地資料交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Train–track data handoff: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「車地資料交接」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Train–track data handoff” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"時間基準不同可造成負延遲假象；漏記排隊會使快速單元測試無法預測整合表現。回到「車地資料交接」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Different clock references can create apparently negative delays; omitted queues prevent fast unit tests from predicting integrated performance. Trace the input chain for train–track data handoff. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：各階段串行且時間確定，沒有平行重疊或隨機尾端。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Deterministic serial stages without overlap or random latency tails.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"時間基準不同可造成負延遲假象；漏記排隊會使快速單元測試無法預測整合表現。回到「車地資料交接」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Different clock references can create apparently negative delays; omitted queues prevent fast unit tests from predicting integrated performance. Trace the input chain for train–track data handoff. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「車地資料交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Train–track data handoff\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","時間基準不同可造成負延遲假象；漏記排隊會使快速單元測試無法預測整合表現。","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Different clock references can create apparently negative delays; omitted queues prevent fast unit tests from predicting integrated performance.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"時間基準不同可造成負延遲假象；漏記排隊會使快速單元測試無法預測整合表現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Different clock references can create apparently negative delays; omitted queues prevent fast unit tests from predicting integrated performance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b371-v16-s3","title":"模式轉換可達性與版本相容需求矩陣","titleEn":"Reachability of mode transitions & Version-compatibility requirement matrix","description":"本階段聚焦「模式轉換可達性」與「版本相容需求矩陣」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Reachability of mode transitions\" and \"Version-compatibility requirement matrix\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b371-v16-17","title":"模式轉換可達性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Reachability of mode transitions: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「模式轉換可達性」如何影響歐洲列車控制系統整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Reachability of mode transitions” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “European Train Control System integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元在抽象狀態機中檢查合法轉換與拒絕轉換，不把版本名稱相同當作所有行為相容的證據。布林狀態組合隨變數個數指數成長，這說明逐一人工檢查很快失去效率。可達性約束能排除不可能組合，但刪除條件必須有證據；安全性質通常針對所有可達狀態，而非幾個畫面上看起來合理的狀態。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：未限制的布林笛卡兒積；實際可達狀態通常較少，但需另證明。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「模式轉換可達性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Check allowed and rejected transitions in an abstract state machine, without treating a shared version name as proof that every behaviour is compatible. Boolean combinations grow exponentially with variable count, explaining why manual enumeration soon becomes ineffective. Reachability constraints can eliminate impossible combinations, but each exclusion needs justification. Safety properties normally concern every reachable state rather than a few states that look plausible on a display. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Unconstrained Boolean Cartesian product; actual reachability can be smaller but must be established separately. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Reachability of mode transitions” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits.","failure":"常見誤解：「狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「模式轉換可達性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Reachability of mode transitions”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-17-k1","title":"模式轉換可達性","titleEn":"Reachability of mode transitions","text":"本單元在抽象狀態機中檢查合法轉換與拒絕轉換，不把版本名稱相同當作所有行為相容的證據。布林狀態組合隨變數個數指數成長，這說明逐一人工檢查很快失去效率。","textEn":"Check allowed and rejected transitions in an abstract state machine, without treating a shared version name as proof that every behaviour is compatible. Boolean combinations grow exponentially with variable count, explaining why manual enumeration soon becomes ineffective.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模式轉換可達性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Reachability of mode transitions\" is correct?","options":["狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","本單元在抽象狀態機中檢查合法轉換與拒絕轉換，不把版本名稱相同當作所有行為相容的證據。"],"optionsEn":["Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Check allowed and rejected transitions in an abstract state machine, without treating a shared version name as proof that every behaviour is compatible."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元在抽象狀態機中檢查合法轉換與拒絕轉換，不把版本名稱相同當作所有行為相容的證據。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Check allowed and rejected transitions in an abstract state machine, without treating a shared version name as proof that every behaviour is compatible. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b371-v16-18","title":"模式轉換可達性：定量估算","titleEn":"Reachability of mode transitions: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「模式轉換可達性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Reachability of mode transitions” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。公式 y=2**bits，代入得 y=256 states。邊界：未限制的布林笛卡兒積；實際可達狀態通常較少，但需另證明。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits. Formula y=2**bits gives y=256 states. Boundary: Unconstrained Boolean Cartesian product; actual reachability can be smaller but must be established separately. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。公式 y=2**bits，代入得 y=256 states。邊界：未限制的布林笛卡兒積；實際可達狀態通常較少，但需另證明。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits. Formula y=2**bits gives y=256 states. Boundary: Unconstrained Boolean Cartesian product; actual reachability can be smaller but must be established separately.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「模式轉換可達性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Reachability of mode transitions\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致","完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.","Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b371-v16-19","title":"模式轉換可達性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Reachability of mode transitions: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「模式轉換可達性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Reachability of mode transitions” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。以「模式轉換可達性」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states. For reachability of mode transitions, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把布林變數數量 bits 從 8 改成 9 bits（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 256 變為 512 states。先說明「模式轉換可達性」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only number of Boolean state variables bits from 8 to 9 bits (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 256 to 512 states. Explain the causal direction for reachability of mode transitions, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。以「模式轉換可達性」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states. For reachability of mode transitions, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把布林變數數量 bits 從 8 改成 9 bits（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 256 變為 512 states。先說明「模式轉換可達性」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only number of Boolean state variables bits from 8 to 9 bits (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 256 to 512 states. Explain the causal direction for reachability of mode transitions, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「模式轉換可達性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Reachability of mode transitions\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。","封包剛收到就代表其中位置一定是現在的位置"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states.","A newly received packet always contains the present position."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b371-v16-20","title":"模式轉換可達性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Reachability of mode transitions: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「模式轉換可達性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Reachability of mode transitions” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。回到「模式轉換可達性」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races. Trace the input chain for reachability of mode transitions. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：未限制的布林笛卡兒積；實際可達狀態通常較少，但需另證明。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Unconstrained Boolean Cartesian product; actual reachability can be smaller but must be established separately.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。回到「模式轉換可達性」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races. Trace the input chain for reachability of mode transitions. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模式轉換可達性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Reachability of mode transitions\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b371-v16-21","title":"版本相容需求矩陣：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Version-compatibility requirement matrix: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「版本相容需求矩陣」如何影響歐洲列車控制系統整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Version-compatibility requirement matrix” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “European Train Control System integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元把車載版本、地面版本與功能需求分別列出，避免只測一種搭配就推論全網互通。測試覆蓋率只對已定義的分母有意義。需求、狀態、轉移與危害各有不同分母，執行很多正常案例仍可能漏掉罕見但重要的交接；同一案例重跑多次不會自動增加獨立需求的覆蓋。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「版本相容需求矩陣」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"List onboard version, trackside version and functional requirements separately, avoiding network-wide interoperability claims from testing one combination. Coverage is meaningful only relative to its defined denominator. Requirements, states, transitions and hazards have different denominators. Many normal cases can still omit a rare but important handoff, and repeating one case does not automatically cover additional independent requirements. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Version-compatibility requirement matrix” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases.","failure":"常見誤解：「測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「版本相容需求矩陣」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Version-compatibility requirement matrix”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-21-k1","title":"版本相容需求矩陣","titleEn":"Version-compatibility requirement matrix","text":"本單元把車載版本、地面版本與功能需求分別列出，避免只測一種搭配就推論全網互通。測試覆蓋率只對已定義的分母有意義。","textEn":"List onboard version, trackside version and functional requirements separately, avoiding network-wide interoperability claims from testing one combination. Coverage is meaningful only relative to its defined denominator.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「版本相容需求矩陣」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Version-compatibility requirement matrix\" is correct?","options":["本單元把車載版本、地面版本與功能需求分別列出，避免只測一種搭配就推論全網互通。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘"],"optionsEn":["List onboard version, trackside version and functional requirements separately, avoiding network-wide interoperability claims from testing one combination.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元把車載版本、地面版本與功能需求分別列出，避免只測一種搭配就推論全網互通。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"List onboard version, trackside version and functional requirements separately, avoiding network-wide interoperability claims from testing one combination. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b371-v16-22","title":"版本相容需求矩陣：定量估算","titleEn":"Version-compatibility requirement matrix: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「版本相容需求矩陣」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Version-compatibility requirement matrix” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。公式 y=tested/total，代入得 y=0.8 1。邊界：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Formula y=tested/total gives y=0.8 1. Boundary: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。公式 y=tested/total，代入得 y=0.8 1。邊界：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Formula y=tested/total gives y=0.8 1. Boundary: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「版本相容需求矩陣」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Version-compatibility requirement matrix\", which statement holds?","options":["所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果","原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。","速度提高一成時停止距離也必定只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases.","Increasing speed by ten percent always increases stopping distance by exactly ten percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b371-v16-23","title":"版本相容需求矩陣：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Version-compatibility requirement matrix: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「版本相容需求矩陣」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Version-compatibility requirement matrix” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。以「版本相容需求矩陣」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. For version-compatibility requirement matrix, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把已執行案例 tested 從 72 改成 73 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.8 變為 0.811111 1。先說明「版本相容需求矩陣」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only executed cases tested from 72 to 73 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.8 to 0.811111 1. Explain the causal direction for version-compatibility requirement matrix, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。以「版本相容需求矩陣」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. For version-compatibility requirement matrix, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把已執行案例 tested 從 72 改成 73 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.8 變為 0.811111 1。先說明「版本相容需求矩陣」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only executed cases tested from 72 to 73 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.8 to 0.811111 1. Explain the causal direction for version-compatibility requirement matrix, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「版本相容需求矩陣」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Version-compatibility requirement matrix\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","短距離校正準確就能保證長距離里程也完全準確","建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Accurate short-distance calibration guarantees perfectly accurate long-distance odometry.","Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b371-v16-24","title":"版本相容需求矩陣：失效診斷","titleEn":"Version-compatibility requirement matrix: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「版本相容需求矩陣」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Version-compatibility requirement matrix” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。回到「版本相容需求矩陣」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Trace the input chain for version-compatibility requirement matrix. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。回到「版本相容需求矩陣」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Trace the input chain for version-compatibility requirement matrix. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「版本相容需求矩陣」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Version-compatibility requirement matrix\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘"],"optionsEn":["Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product."],"answer":0,"explanation":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b371-v16-s4","title":"介面失配頂事件與測試記錄時間對齊","titleEn":"Top event for interface mismatch & Aligning integration-test clocks","description":"本階段聚焦「介面失配頂事件」與「測試記錄時間對齊」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Top event for interface mismatch\" and \"Aligning integration-test clocks\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b371-v16-25","title":"介面失配頂事件：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Top event for interface mismatch: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「介面失配頂事件」如何影響歐洲列車控制系統整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Top event for interface mismatch” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “European Train Control System integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元把資料語意與設定檔錯配作為不同候選原因，先建立失效邏輯再討論假想機率。只要任一支路失效就產生頂事件時，需計算聯集而不是把兩機率相乘。獨立假設允許扣掉交集的乘積，若共享電源、環境或軟體則交集另有結構；事件樹和失效樹必須保持同一任務時間。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：兩事件獨立且機率屬同一任務期間，並非每小時危險失效率。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「介面失配頂事件」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Treat semantic mismatch and configuration mismatch as distinct candidate causes, defining fault logic before assigning hypothetical probabilities. When either branch can trigger the top event, the relevant probability is a union rather than a product. Independence permits the intersection to be written as a product; shared power, environment or software changes that intersection. Event and fault trees must use the same mission duration. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Two independent events over one mission interval, not a dangerous-failure rate per hour. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Top event for interface mismatch” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：事件一機率 p1=0.001 1；事件二機率 p2=0.002 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: event one probability p1=0.001 1; event two probability p2=0.002 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「介面失配頂事件」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Top event for interface mismatch”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-25-k1","title":"介面失配頂事件","titleEn":"Top event for interface mismatch","text":"本單元把資料語意與設定檔錯配作為不同候選原因，先建立失效邏輯再討論假想機率。只要任一支路失效就產生頂事件時，需計算聯集而不是把兩機率相乘。","textEn":"Treat semantic mismatch and configuration mismatch as distinct candidate causes, defining fault logic before assigning hypothetical probabilities. When either branch can trigger the top event, the relevant probability is a union rather than a product.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「介面失配頂事件」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Top event for interface mismatch\" is correct?","options":["任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘","本單元把資料語意與設定檔錯配作為不同候選原因，先建立失效邏輯再討論假想機率。","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致"],"optionsEn":["If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product.","Treat semantic mismatch and configuration mismatch as distinct candidate causes, defining fault logic before assigning hypothetical probabilities.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元把資料語意與設定檔錯配作為不同候選原因，先建立失效邏輯再討論假想機率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Treat semantic mismatch and configuration mismatch as distinct candidate causes, defining fault logic before assigning hypothetical probabilities. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b371-v16-26","title":"介面失配頂事件：定量估算","titleEn":"Top event for interface mismatch: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「介面失配頂事件」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Top event for interface mismatch” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：事件一機率 p1=0.001 1；事件二機率 p2=0.002 1。公式 y=p1+p2-p1*p2，代入得 y=0.002998 1。邊界：兩事件獨立且機率屬同一任務期間，並非每小時危險失效率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: event one probability p1=0.001 1; event two probability p2=0.002 1. Formula y=p1+p2-p1*p2 gives y=0.002998 1. Boundary: Two independent events over one mission interval, not a dangerous-failure rate per hour. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先畫頂事件邏輯再代機率，明列共享資源並檢查事件時間窗是否一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw top-event logic before inserting probabilities, list shared resources, and check consistent time windows.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：事件一機率 p1=0.001 1；事件二機率 p2=0.002 1。公式 y=p1+p2-p1*p2，代入得 y=0.002998 1。邊界：兩事件獨立且機率屬同一任務期間，並非每小時危險失效率。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: event one probability p1=0.001 1; event two probability p2=0.002 1. Formula y=p1+p2-p1*p2 gives y=0.002998 1. Boundary: Two independent events over one mission interval, not a dangerous-failure rate per hour.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「介面失配頂事件」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Top event for interface mismatch\", which statement holds?","options":["完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零","封包剛收到就代表其中位置一定是現在的位置","原創假想教學輸入：事件一機率 p1=0.001 1；事件二機率 p2=0.002 1。"],"optionsEn":["Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero.","A newly received packet always contains the present position.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: event one probability p1=0.001 1; event two probability p2=0.002 1."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：事件一機率 p1=0.001 1；事件二機率 p2=0.002 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: event one probability p1=0.001 1; event two probability p2=0.002 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b371-v16-27","title":"介面失配頂事件：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Top event for interface mismatch: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「介面失配頂事件」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Top event for interface mismatch” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先畫頂事件邏輯再代機率，明列共享資源並檢查事件時間窗是否一致。以「介面失配頂事件」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw top-event logic before inserting probabilities, list shared resources, and check consistent time windows. For top event for interface mismatch, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把事件一機率 p1 從 0.001 改成 0.0011 1（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.002998 變為 0.0030978 1。先說明「介面失配頂事件」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only event one probability p1 from 0.001 to 0.0011 1 (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.002998 to 0.0030978 1. Explain the causal direction for top event for interface mismatch, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：把聯集誤寫成交集會低估危險；混合年度機率與每小時機率則使結果失去量綱意義。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing a union with an intersection understates risk; mixing annual and hourly probabilities destroys the intended meaning. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先畫頂事件邏輯再代機率，明列共享資源並檢查事件時間窗是否一致。以「介面失配頂事件」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Draw top-event logic before inserting probabilities, list shared resources, and check consistent time windows. For top event for interface mismatch, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把事件一機率 p1 從 0.001 改成 0.0011 1（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.002998 變為 0.0030978 1。先說明「介面失配頂事件」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only event one probability p1 from 0.001 to 0.0011 1 (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.002998 to 0.0030978 1. Explain the causal direction for top event for interface mismatch, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「介面失配頂事件」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Top event for interface mismatch\"?","options":["先畫頂事件邏輯再代機率，明列共享資源並檢查事件時間窗是否一致。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短"],"optionsEn":["Draw top-event logic before inserting probabilities, list shared resources, and check consistent time windows.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay."],"answer":0,"explanation":"先畫頂事件邏輯再代機率，明列共享資源並檢查事件時間窗是否一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw top-event logic before inserting probabilities, list shared resources, and check consistent time windows. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b371-v16-28","title":"介面失配頂事件：失效診斷","titleEn":"Top event for interface mismatch: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「介面失配頂事件」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Top event for interface mismatch” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把聯集誤寫成交集會低估危險；混合年度機率與每小時機率則使結果失去量綱意義。回到「介面失配頂事件」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing a union with an intersection understates risk; mixing annual and hourly probabilities destroys the intended meaning. Trace the input chain for top event for interface mismatch. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：兩事件獨立且機率屬同一任務期間，並非每小時危險失效率。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Two independent events over one mission interval, not a dangerous-failure rate per hour.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把聯集誤寫成交集會低估危險；混合年度機率與每小時機率則使結果失去量綱意義。回到「介面失配頂事件」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Confusing a union with an intersection understates risk; mixing annual and hourly probabilities destroys the intended meaning. Trace the input chain for top event for interface mismatch. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「介面失配頂事件」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Top event for interface mismatch\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把聯集誤寫成交集會低估危險；混合年度機率與每小時機率則使結果失去量綱意義。","測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Confusing a union with an intersection understates risk; mixing annual and hourly probabilities destroys the intended meaning.","Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把聯集誤寫成交集會低估危險；混合年度機率與每小時機率則使結果失去量綱意義。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing a union with an intersection understates risk; mixing annual and hourly probabilities destroys the intended meaning. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b371-v16-29","title":"測試記錄時間對齊：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Aligning integration-test clocks: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「測試記錄時間對齊」如何影響歐洲列車控制系統整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Aligning integration-test clocks” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “European Train Control System integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元比較車載、地面和測試儀紀錄的時間差，避免把儀器時基誤差當成系統反應延遲。時鐘頻率偏差會隨時間累積成時間差，校時瞬間的偏移與之不同。多系統事件排序若依不同時鐘，可能把因果順序顛倒；校時跳變又會使量測區間長度失真，所以需記錄時鐘品質與校正事件。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：固定頻率偏差的線性累積，忽略溫度漂移與校時伺服動態。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測試記錄時間對齊」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compare timestamps from onboard equipment, wayside equipment and test instruments, avoiding confusion between reference-clock error and system response delay. Clock frequency error accumulates into time offset and differs from initial synchronization offset. Ordering multisystem events on different clocks can reverse apparent causality. Synchronization jumps can distort interval lengths, so clock quality and correction events must be recorded. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Linear accumulation at fixed frequency offset; temperature drift and synchronization-servo dynamics are omitted. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Aligning integration-test clocks” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測試記錄時間對齊」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Aligning integration-test clocks”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-29-k1","title":"測試記錄時間對齊","titleEn":"Aligning integration-test clocks","text":"本單元比較車載、地面和測試儀紀錄的時間差，避免把儀器時基誤差當成系統反應延遲。時鐘頻率偏差會隨時間累積成時間差，校時瞬間的偏移與之不同。","textEn":"Compare timestamps from onboard equipment, wayside equipment and test instruments, avoiding confusion between reference-clock error and system response delay. Clock frequency error accumulates into time offset and differs from initial synchronization offset.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測試記錄時間對齊」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Aligning integration-test clocks\" is correct?","options":["測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致","所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果","本單元比較車載、地面和測試儀紀錄的時間差，避免把儀器時基誤差當成系統反應延遲。"],"optionsEn":["Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.","All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results.","Compare timestamps from onboard equipment, wayside equipment and test instruments, avoiding confusion between reference-clock error and system response delay."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元比較車載、地面和測試儀紀錄的時間差，避免把儀器時基誤差當成系統反應延遲。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compare timestamps from onboard equipment, wayside equipment and test instruments, avoiding confusion between reference-clock error and system response delay. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b371-v16-30","title":"測試記錄時間對齊：定量估算","titleEn":"Aligning integration-test clocks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測試記錄時間對齊」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Aligning integration-test clocks” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。公式 y=drift*1e-6*duration，代入得 y=0.072 s。邊界：固定頻率偏差的線性累積，忽略溫度漂移與校時伺服動態。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s. Formula y=drift*1e-6*duration gives y=0.072 s. Boundary: Linear accumulation at fixed frequency offset; temperature drift and synchronization-servo dynamics are omitted. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。公式 y=drift*1e-6*duration，代入得 y=0.072 s。邊界：固定頻率偏差的線性累積，忽略溫度漂移與校時伺服動態。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s. Formula y=drift*1e-6*duration gives y=0.072 s. Boundary: Linear accumulation at fixed frequency offset; temperature drift and synchronization-servo dynamics are omitted.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測試記錄時間對齊」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Aligning integration-test clocks\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。","速度提高一成時停止距離也必定只增加一成","短距離校正準確就能保證長距離里程也完全準確"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s.","Increasing speed by ten percent always increases stopping distance by exactly ten percent.","Accurate short-distance calibration guarantees perfectly accurate long-distance odometry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：時鐘頻率偏差 drift=20 ppm；未校時期間 duration=3600 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: clock frequency offset drift=20 ppm; unsynchronized interval duration=3600 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b371-v16-31","title":"測試記錄時間對齊：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Aligning integration-test clocks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測試記錄時間對齊」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Aligning integration-test clocks” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。以「測試記錄時間對齊」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump. For aligning integration-test clocks, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把未校時期間 duration 從 3600 改成 3960 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.072 變為 0.0792 s。先說明「測試記錄時間對齊」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only unsynchronized interval duration from 3600 to 3960 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.072 to 0.0792 s. Explain the causal direction for aligning integration-test clocks, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。以「測試記錄時間對齊」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump. For aligning integration-test clocks, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把未校時期間 duration 從 3600 改成 3960 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.072 變為 0.0792 s。先說明「測試記錄時間對齊」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only unsynchronized interval duration from 3600 to 3960 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.072 to 0.0792 s. Explain the causal direction for aligning integration-test clocks, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測試記錄時間對齊」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Aligning integration-test clocks\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用獨立時間基準比較多個時刻的偏移，從斜率分辨頻率誤差與一次性跳變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare offsets at several times against an independent reference, using slope to distinguish frequency error from a one-time jump. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b371-v16-32","title":"測試記錄時間對齊：失效診斷","titleEn":"Aligning integration-test clocks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測試記錄時間對齊」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Aligning integration-test clocks” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。回到「測試記錄時間對齊」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay. Trace the input chain for aligning integration-test clocks. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：固定頻率偏差的線性累積，忽略溫度漂移與校時伺服動態。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Linear accumulation at fixed frequency offset; temperature drift and synchronization-servo dynamics are omitted.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「測試開始時時鐘一致就能保證整天時間戳都一致」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Clocks aligned at test start remain aligned for the entire day.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。回到「測試記錄時間對齊」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay. Trace the input chain for aligning integration-test clocks. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測試記錄時間對齊」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Aligning integration-test clocks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果","只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results.","Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只對齊開始時刻卻忽略頻率漂移，會讓長測試中的事件逐漸錯位，並誤判通訊延遲。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Aligning only the initial instant leaves frequency drift uncorrected, progressively misaligning events and suggesting false network delay. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b371-v16-s5","title":"跨版本回歸測試與互通試驗推論範圍","titleEn":"Cross-version regression testing & Scope of interoperability inference","description":"本階段聚焦「跨版本回歸測試」與「互通試驗推論範圍」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cross-version regression testing\" and \"Scope of interoperability inference\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b371-v16-33","title":"跨版本回歸測試：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cross-version regression testing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「跨版本回歸測試」如何影響歐洲列車控制系統整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cross-version regression testing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “European Train Control System integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元為每種版本組合保留環境還原與資料核對時間，明確追蹤變更後哪些證據需要重新取得。測試工時包含案例執行與環境設定、資料復原及證據整理。平行化只有在資源和狀態真正獨立時有效；把多個會修改同一狀態的測試同時執行，可能造成結果不可重現，表面節省時間卻增加診斷成本。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：確定平均案例時間的串行估算，未含故障重測與資源衝突。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「跨版本回歸測試」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Budget restoration and data checks for every version combination, explicitly tracking which evidence must be regenerated after a change. Test effort includes case execution, setup, state restoration and evidence handling. Parallelism helps only when resources and state are genuinely independent. Concurrent tests modifying one shared state can become irreproducible, apparently saving execution time while increasing diagnostic cost. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Serial estimate with deterministic mean case time; failure reruns and resource conflicts are excluded. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cross-version regression testing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：測試案例數 cases=120 cases；平均案例時間 minutes=8 min/case；設定與恢復時間 setup=180 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: test cases cases=120 cases; mean case duration minutes=8 min/case; setup and recovery time setup=180 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「跨版本回歸測試」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cross-version regression testing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-33-k1","title":"跨版本回歸測試","titleEn":"Cross-version regression testing","text":"本單元為每種版本組合保留環境還原與資料核對時間，明確追蹤變更後哪些證據需要重新取得。測試工時包含案例執行與環境設定、資料復原及證據整理。","textEn":"Budget restoration and data checks for every version combination, explicitly tracking which evidence must be regenerated after a change. Test effort includes case execution, setup, state restoration and evidence handling.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「跨版本回歸測試」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cross-version regression testing\" is correct?","options":["本單元為每種版本組合保留環境還原與資料核對時間，明確追蹤變更後哪些證據需要重新取得。","所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果","完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零"],"optionsEn":["Budget restoration and data checks for every version combination, explicitly tracking which evidence must be regenerated after a change.","All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results.","Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元為每種版本組合保留環境還原與資料核對時間，明確追蹤變更後哪些證據需要重新取得。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Budget restoration and data checks for every version combination, explicitly tracking which evidence must be regenerated after a change. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b371-v16-34","title":"跨版本回歸測試：定量估算","titleEn":"Cross-version regression testing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「跨版本回歸測試」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cross-version regression testing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：測試案例數 cases=120 cases；平均案例時間 minutes=8 min/case；設定與恢復時間 setup=180 min。公式 y=(cases*minutes+setup)/60，代入得 y=19 h。邊界：確定平均案例時間的串行估算，未含故障重測與資源衝突。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: test cases cases=120 cases; mean case duration minutes=8 min/case; setup and recovery time setup=180 min. Formula y=(cases*minutes+setup)/60 gives y=19 h. Boundary: Serial estimate with deterministic mean case time; failure reruns and resource conflicts are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐案記錄前置狀態、執行時間與復原時間，分開列出正常完成和失敗重測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record preconditions, execution and restoration for every case, separating normal completion from failure reruns.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：測試案例數 cases=120 cases；平均案例時間 minutes=8 min/case；設定與恢復時間 setup=180 min。公式 y=(cases*minutes+setup)/60，代入得 y=19 h。邊界：確定平均案例時間的串行估算，未含故障重測與資源衝突。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: test cases cases=120 cases; mean case duration minutes=8 min/case; setup and recovery time setup=180 min. Formula y=(cases*minutes+setup)/60 gives y=19 h. Boundary: Serial estimate with deterministic mean case time; failure reruns and resource conflicts are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「跨版本回歸測試」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cross-version regression testing\", which statement holds?","options":["封包剛收到就代表其中位置一定是現在的位置","原創假想教學輸入：測試案例數 cases=120 cases；平均案例時間 minutes=8 min/case；設定與恢復時間 setup=180 min。","每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短"],"optionsEn":["A newly received packet always contains the present position.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: test cases cases=120 cases; mean case duration minutes=8 min/case; setup and recovery time setup=180 min.","Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：測試案例數 cases=120 cases；平均案例時間 minutes=8 min/case；設定與恢復時間 setup=180 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: test cases cases=120 cases; mean case duration minutes=8 min/case; setup and recovery time setup=180 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b371-v16-35","title":"跨版本回歸測試：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cross-version regression testing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「跨版本回歸測試」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cross-version regression testing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐案記錄前置狀態、執行時間與復原時間，分開列出正常完成和失敗重測。以「跨版本回歸測試」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record preconditions, execution and restoration for every case, separating normal completion from failure reruns. For cross-version regression testing, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把測試案例數 cases 從 120 改成 121 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 19 變為 19.1333 h。先說明「跨版本回歸測試」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only test cases cases from 120 to 121 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 19 to 19.1333 h. Explain the causal direction for cross-version regression testing, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：省略復原步驟會讓前案狀態污染後案，僅報告成功案例時間則低估總測試成本。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitted restoration contaminates later tests with earlier state; reporting only successful durations understates total effort. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐案記錄前置狀態、執行時間與復原時間，分開列出正常完成和失敗重測。以「跨版本回歸測試」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Record preconditions, execution and restoration for every case, separating normal completion from failure reruns. For cross-version regression testing, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把測試案例數 cases 從 120 改成 121 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 19 變為 19.1333 h。先說明「跨版本回歸測試」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only test cases cases from 120 to 121 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 19 to 19.1333 h. Explain the causal direction for cross-version regression testing, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「跨版本回歸測試」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cross-version regression testing\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","逐案記錄前置狀態、執行時間與復原時間，分開列出正常完成和失敗重測。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Record preconditions, execution and restoration for every case, separating normal completion from failure reruns."],"answer":2,"explanation":"逐案記錄前置狀態、執行時間與復原時間，分開列出正常完成和失敗重測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record preconditions, execution and restoration for every case, separating normal completion from failure reruns. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b371-v16-36","title":"跨版本回歸測試：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cross-version regression testing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「跨版本回歸測試」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cross-version regression testing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"省略復原步驟會讓前案狀態污染後案，僅報告成功案例時間則低估總測試成本。回到「跨版本回歸測試」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitted restoration contaminates later tests with earlier state; reporting only successful durations understates total effort. Trace the input chain for cross-version regression testing. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：確定平均案例時間的串行估算，未含故障重測與資源衝突。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Serial estimate with deterministic mean case time; failure reruns and resource conflicts are excluded.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"省略復原步驟會讓前案狀態污染後案，僅報告成功案例時間則低估總測試成本。回到「跨版本回歸測試」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Omitted restoration contaminates later tests with earlier state; reporting only successful durations understates total effort. Trace the input chain for cross-version regression testing. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「跨版本回歸測試」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cross-version regression testing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["省略復原步驟會讓前案狀態污染後案，僅報告成功案例時間則低估總測試成本。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零"],"optionsEn":["Omitted restoration contaminates later tests with earlier state; reporting only successful durations understates total effort.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero."],"answer":0,"explanation":"省略復原步驟會讓前案狀態污染後案，僅報告成功案例時間則低估總測試成本。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitted restoration contaminates later tests with earlier state; reporting only successful durations understates total effort. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b371-v16-37","title":"互通試驗推論範圍：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Scope of interoperability inference: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「互通試驗推論範圍」如何影響歐洲列車控制系統整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Scope of interoperability inference” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “European Train Control System integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元把成功試驗限制在已測功能與版本集合，說明零失敗紀錄不能外推到未測國別或設備。零次觀察到失效不代表真實失效機率為零。獨立伯努利試驗可由全數成功的機率反推單側上界，試驗數增加才會縮小界限；相關測試或只選容易案例會使這個統計推論不再成立，也不能由此宣告達到安全完整性等級。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：獨立同分布二元試驗且觀察零失效，非每小時失效率。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「互通試驗推論範圍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Limit successful-test inference to the tested function and version set, explaining why a zero-failure record does not cover untested national or equipment variants. Zero observed failures does not imply zero true failure probability. Independent Bernoulli trials allow a one-sided upper bound from the probability of all successes, which decreases with sample count. Correlated or selectively easy cases invalidate this inference and cannot establish a safety-integrity level. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Independent identical binary trials with zero observed failures, not an hourly failure rate. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Scope of interoperability inference” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：獨立試驗次數 tests=300 independent trials；單側信賴水準 confidence=0.95 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent trial count tests=300 independent trials; one-sided confidence level confidence=0.95 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「互通試驗推論範圍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Scope of interoperability inference”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-37-k1","title":"互通試驗推論範圍","titleEn":"Scope of interoperability inference","text":"本單元把成功試驗限制在已測功能與版本集合，說明零失敗紀錄不能外推到未測國別或設備。零次觀察到失效不代表真實失效機率為零。","textEn":"Limit successful-test inference to the tested function and version set, explaining why a zero-failure record does not cover untested national or equipment variants. Zero observed failures does not imply zero true failure probability.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「互通試驗推論範圍」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Scope of interoperability inference\" is correct?","options":["完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零","本單元把成功試驗限制在已測功能與版本集合，說明零失敗紀錄不能外推到未測國別或設備。","速度提高一成時停止距離也必定只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero.","Limit successful-test inference to the tested function and version set, explaining why a zero-failure record does not cover untested national or equipment variants.","Increasing speed by ten percent always increases stopping distance by exactly ten percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元把成功試驗限制在已測功能與版本集合，說明零失敗紀錄不能外推到未測國別或設備。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Limit successful-test inference to the tested function and version set, explaining why a zero-failure record does not cover untested national or equipment variants. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b371-v16-38","title":"互通試驗推論範圍：定量估算","titleEn":"Scope of interoperability inference: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「互通試驗推論範圍」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Scope of interoperability inference” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：獨立試驗次數 tests=300 independent trials；單側信賴水準 confidence=0.95 1。公式 y=1-(1-confidence)**(1/tests)，代入得 y=0.00993608 failure probability。邊界：獨立同分布二元試驗且觀察零失效，非每小時失效率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent trial count tests=300 independent trials; one-sided confidence level confidence=0.95 1. Formula y=1-(1-confidence)**(1/tests) gives y=0.00993608 failure probability. Boundary: Independent identical binary trials with zero observed failures, not an hourly failure rate. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對案例獨立性與抽樣範圍，保留所有失敗紀錄，再說明統計界限對哪一類情境有效。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Audit independence and sampling scope, retain all failures, and state the scenario population to which the bound applies.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：獨立試驗次數 tests=300 independent trials；單側信賴水準 confidence=0.95 1。公式 y=1-(1-confidence)**(1/tests)，代入得 y=0.00993608 failure probability。邊界：獨立同分布二元試驗且觀察零失效，非每小時失效率。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent trial count tests=300 independent trials; one-sided confidence level confidence=0.95 1. Formula y=1-(1-confidence)**(1/tests) gives y=0.00993608 failure probability. Boundary: Independent identical binary trials with zero observed failures, not an hourly failure rate.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「互通試驗推論範圍」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Scope of interoperability inference\", which statement holds?","options":["短距離校正準確就能保證長距離里程也完全準確","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合","原創假想教學輸入：獨立試驗次數 tests=300 independent trials；單側信賴水準 confidence=0.95 1。"],"optionsEn":["Accurate short-distance calibration guarantees perfectly accurate long-distance odometry.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent trial count tests=300 independent trials; one-sided confidence level confidence=0.95 1."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：獨立試驗次數 tests=300 independent trials；單側信賴水準 confidence=0.95 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent trial count tests=300 independent trials; one-sided confidence level confidence=0.95 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b371-v16-39","title":"互通試驗推論範圍：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Scope of interoperability inference: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「互通試驗推論範圍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Scope of interoperability inference” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對案例獨立性與抽樣範圍，保留所有失敗紀錄，再說明統計界限對哪一類情境有效。以「互通試驗推論範圍」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Audit independence and sampling scope, retain all failures, and state the scenario population to which the bound applies. For scope of interoperability inference, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把獨立試驗次數 tests 從 300 改成 301 independent trials（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.00993608 變為 0.00990324 failure probability。先說明「互通試驗推論範圍」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only independent trial count tests from 300 to 301 independent trials (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.00993608 to 0.00990324 failure probability. Explain the causal direction for scope of interoperability inference, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：反覆重跑相同狀態可能沒有增加獨立證據，刪去失敗案例則直接破壞零失效假設。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Repeated identical states may add no independent evidence, while deleting failures invalidates the zero-failure assumption. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對案例獨立性與抽樣範圍，保留所有失敗紀錄，再說明統計界限對哪一類情境有效。以「互通試驗推論範圍」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Audit independence and sampling scope, retain all failures, and state the scenario population to which the bound applies. For scope of interoperability inference, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把獨立試驗次數 tests 從 300 改成 301 independent trials（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.00993608 變為 0.00990324 failure probability。先說明「互通試驗推論範圍」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only independent trial count tests from 300 to 301 independent trials (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.00993608 to 0.00990324 failure probability. Explain the causal direction for scope of interoperability inference, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「互通試驗推論範圍」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Scope of interoperability inference\"?","options":["核對案例獨立性與抽樣範圍，保留所有失敗紀錄，再說明統計界限對哪一類情境有效。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","任一支路故障即失效時總機率等於兩機率相乘"],"optionsEn":["Audit independence and sampling scope, retain all failures, and state the scenario population to which the bound applies.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","If either branch failure is sufficient, total failure probability equals their product."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對案例獨立性與抽樣範圍，保留所有失敗紀錄，再說明統計界限對哪一類情境有效。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Audit independence and sampling scope, retain all failures, and state the scenario population to which the bound applies. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b371-v16-40","title":"互通試驗推論範圍：失效診斷","titleEn":"Scope of interoperability inference: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b371-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「互通試驗推論範圍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Scope of interoperability inference” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"反覆重跑相同狀態可能沒有增加獨立證據，刪去失敗案例則直接破壞零失效假設。回到「互通試驗推論範圍」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Repeated identical states may add no independent evidence, while deleting failures invalidates the zero-failure assumption. Trace the input chain for scope of interoperability inference. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：獨立同分布二元試驗且觀察零失效，非每小時失效率。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Independent identical binary trials with zero observed failures, not an hourly failure rate.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「完成很多次沒有故障的測試就能證明故障機率為零」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Many failure-free tests prove that the failure probability is zero.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b371-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"反覆重跑相同狀態可能沒有增加獨立證據，刪去失敗案例則直接破壞零失效假設。回到「互通試驗推論範圍」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Repeated identical states may add no independent evidence, while deleting failures invalidates the zero-failure assumption. Trace the input chain for scope of interoperability inference. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]},{"id":"b371-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「互通試驗推論範圍」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Scope of interoperability inference\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","反覆重跑相同狀態可能沒有增加獨立證據，刪去失敗案例則直接破壞零失效假設。","速度提高一成時停止距離也必定只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Repeated identical states may add no independent evidence, while deleting failures invalidates the zero-failure assumption.","Increasing speed by ten percent always increases stopping distance by exactly ten percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"反覆重跑相同狀態可能沒有增加獨立證據，刪去失敗案例則直接破壞零失效假設。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Repeated identical states may add no independent evidence, while deleting failures invalidates the zero-failure assumption. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-rams-2002","v16s-era-ccs","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-gotthard-reference","v16s-elizabeth-reference"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b371-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b371-en.svg"}};
